    "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR removes Minisat as a dependency for the `udb` Ruby gems, standardizing SAT solving on Z3 and adjusting tests/tooling accordingly to account for Z3 performance characteristics.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Removed `ruby-minisat` (and related `require`s/RBIs) from the Ruby gems and devcontainer.\n- Updated logic SAT/equivalence APIs to use Z3 and thread `cfg_arch` through satisfiable/equivalence checks.\n- Throttled randomly-generated boolean-expression regression tests and regenerated Sorbet RBIs / build scripts.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 8 out of 20 changed files in this pull request and generated 4 comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/udb.gemspec | Drops `ruby-minisat` gem dependency. |\r\n| Gemfile.lock | Removes `ruby-minisat` from the lockfile. |\r\n| .devcontainer/Dockerfile | Removes `minisat` OS package. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/sorbet/tapioca/require.rb | Removes `require \"minisat\"`; keeps `z3`. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb-gen/sorbet/tapioca/require.rb | Removes `require \"minisat\"` from generator gem Tapioca requires. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/udb/logic.rb | Replaces Minisat-based solving with Z3; updates SAT/equivalence APIs to accept `cfg_arch`. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/udb/condition.rb | Removes `require \"minisat\"`. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/test/test_logic.rb | Threads `cfg_arch` into satisfiable/equivalence checks; throttles random tests. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/test/boolean_expressions.json | Removes some large random expressions to reduce Z3 runtime. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/sorbet/rbi/dsl/udb/architecture.rbi | Adds register-file-related method signatures. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb-gen/sorbet/rbi/dsl/udb/architecture.rbi | Mirrors register-file-related method signatures in generated gem. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/sorbet/rbi/annotations/minitest.rbi | Removes `assert_send` signature. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/idlc/sorbet/rbi/annotations/minitest.rbi | Removes `assert_send` signature. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/sorbet/rbi/ruby-minisat.rbi | Deletes Minisat RBI definitions. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb-gen/lib/sorbet/rbi/ruby-minisat.rbi | Removes pointer to the deleted Minisat RBI file. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb-gen/sorbet/rbi/gems/udb@0.1.0.rbi | Regenerated RBI; still contains Minisat stubs/references (needs cleanup). |\r\n| bin/chore | Makes regress generation idempotent; runs Ruby type-def generation; fixes path for `cd`. |\r\n| bin/.container-tag | Bumps devcontainer tag version. |\n</details>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Files not reviewed (7)</summary>\n\n* **tools/ruby-gems/idlc/sorbet/rbi/annotations/minitest.rbi**: Language not supported\n* **tools/ruby-gems/udb-gen/lib/sorbet/rbi/ruby-minisat.rbi**: Language not supported\n* **tools/ruby-gems/udb-gen/sorbet/rbi/dsl/udb/architecture.rbi**: Language not supported\n* **tools/ruby-gems/udb-gen/sorbet/rbi/gems/udb@0.1.0.rbi**: Language not supported\n* **tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/sorbet/rbi/ruby-minisat.rbi**: Language not supported\n* **tools/ruby-gems/udb/sorbet/rbi/annotations/minitest.rbi**: Language not supported\n* **tools/ruby-gems/udb/sorbet/rbi/dsl/udb/architecture.rbi**: Language not supported\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Comments suppressed due to low confidence (1)</summary>\n\n**tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/udb/logic.rb:3165**\n* `LogicNode#equivalent?` constructs the biconditional incorrectly. The second clause currently uses `(!self || self)`, which is a tautology, so the method effectively only checks `self -> other` (one direction) rather than true equivalence. This will produce false positives where `self` implies `other` but `other` does not imply `self`. The second OR should use `(!other || self)` (or equivalent logic) to check both directions.\n```\n    sig { params(other: LogicNode, cfg_arch: ConfiguredArchitecture).returns(T::Boolean) }\n    def equivalent?(other, cfg_arch)\n      # equivalent (A <=> B) if the biconditional is true:\n      #   (A -> B) && (B -> A)\n      # or, expressed without implication:\n      #   (!A || B) && (!B || A)\n\n      # equivalence is a tautology iff ~(A <=> B) is a contradiction,\n      # i.e., !(A <=> B) is UNSATISFIABLE\n      #       !((!A || B) && (!B || A)) is UNSATISFIABLE\n\n      r = self\n      other = other\n      contradiction = LogicNode.new(\n        LogicNodeType::Not,\n        [\n          LogicNode.new(\n            LogicNodeType::And,\n            [\n              LogicNode.new(\n                LogicNodeType::Or,\n                [\n                  LogicNode.new(LogicNodeType::Not, [r]),\n                  other\n                ]\n              ),\n              LogicNode.new(\n                LogicNodeType::Or,\n                [\n                  LogicNode.new(LogicNodeType::Not, [r]),\n                  self\n                ]\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/riscv/riscv-unified-db/new/main/.github/instructions?filename=*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
